NAME
    rmdir - remove an empty directory

SYNOPSIS
    rmdir path

DESCRIPTION
    Removes a directory that holds nothing but "." and ".." (deleted
    files do not count, so a directory emptied with del can go). Quiet
    on success; "not an empty directory" on any failure: not empty, but
    also not found, not a directory, or ".", ".." or the root. Its
    sectors are not reclaimed (no PACK yet). rmdir is a shell built-in
    (the RMDIR syscall, 9).

EXAMPLES
    rmdir /T/SUB
    rmdir SUB

NOTES
    Removed from the P8X version: pack.
    The command is the Y1/OS shell's own (os/y1os.c); the page is
    ported from P8X os/man/rmdir 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
